cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "organism_sim: rule-evolving agents with a routed bus and pre-registered benchmarks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it. Negative results are part of the record."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Davis
    given-names: Devin Phillip
    email: osiris.dnalang@gmail.com
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-20
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/osiris-dnalang/organism_sim
abstract: >-
  Artificial-life simulation of autonomous rule-evolving agents: an XCS-lineage
  Learning Classifier System with a closed s-expression action DSL, a routed
  Payload(content, pressure) message bus with cross-agent credit, and hash-chained
  telemetry. Pre-registered benchmarks with their data: emergent signalling rate
  (18% full, 50 seeds), concept drift on 6-mux (FAIL for the organism layer),
  relay-failure recovery (dead PASS - local trigger 2x faster than a global
  supervisor, 0 false alarms; poisoned FAIL 20/30, CUSUM 24/30).
